| ✅ | TestGlobalMemStoreSize | Reduced version: verifies memstore behavior via RegionMetrics (increase after writes, decrease after flush) instead of internal accounting. 7 checkpoints. |
| 🔄 | TestHBaseTestingUtility | Rechecked 2025-11-18: Confirmed not transformable. All 12 test methods are meta-tests of HBaseTestingUtility framework itself, not HBase functionality: (1) Multi-cluster ZK coordination, (2) Framework lifecycle (start/stop/kill), (3) ZK server management (killing servers, port allocation), (4) MiniDFSCluster lifecycle, (5) Mockito-based unit tests of PortAllocator internals, (6) Port configuration override behavior. Zero transformable HBase functionality - every test validates testing infrastructure, not database operations. |
| ✅ | TestHColumnDescriptorDefaultVersions | Reduced version: 3 tests verify column family version settings via Admin API. HDFS direct verification removed (requires MasterFileSystem access). 5 checkpoints. |
| 🔄 | TestIOFencing | Rechecked 2025-11-18: Confirmed not transformable. Test validates I/O fencing during double-assignment (region on two servers simultaneously). Requires: (1) Custom HRegion subclasses (CompactionBlockerRegion) with CountDownLatch/AtomicInteger to pause/resume compactions mid-execution, (2) HConstants.REGION_IMPL injection into separate JVMs (impossible in ProcessBased), (3) Casting to custom region class and calling stopCompactions()/allowCompactions()/waitForCompactionToBlock(), (4) Direct WAL access (writeCompactionMarker), (5) Direct HStore file list access, (6) expireRegionServerSession() to simulate ZK session expiration. Core value is testing race condition between compaction-in-progress on dying server and region opening on new server - requires in-JVM coordination impossible across process boundaries. |
| 🔄 | TestJMXListener | Rechecked 2025-11-18: Confirmed not suitable for transformation. 3 test methods: (1) testStart() - connects to JMX at specific RMI port and verifies MBean domain (requires knowing JMX port), (2) testStop() - shuts down cluster and verifies JMX connection fails (requires JMX port), (3) testGetRegionServerCoprocessors() - verifies JMXListener coprocessor is loaded via rs.getRegionServer().getRegionServerCoprocessors(). Only testGetRegionServerCoprocessors could be transformed using ServerMetrics.getCoprocessorNames(), but this represents only 1/3 of test value and is trivial coprocessor verification already covered elsewhere. Core test value is JMX connectivity validation across specific ports - JMX ports are allocated internally in each separate ProcessBased JVM and not exposed via any client API. Not worth partial transformation. |
| 🔄 | TestLocalHBaseCluster | Rechecked 2025-11-18: Confirmed not transformable. Single test method (testLocalHBaseCluster) validates LocalHBaseCluster's ability to: (1) Accept custom Master/RS classes via StartMiniClusterOption.builder().masterClass(MyHMaster.class).rsClass(MyHRegionServer.class), (2) getMaster(0)/getRegionServer(0) and cast to custom classes, (3) Call custom methods (echo()) on those instances. ProcessBasedMiniHBaseCluster cannot inject custom classes into separate JVM processes (each process loads from standard HBase distribution), does not provide getMaster()/getRegionServer() (cross-process access), and cannot call custom methods across process boundaries. Test validates testing framework flexibility, not HBase functionality. |
| 🔄 | TestMetaTableAccessor | Rechecked 2025-11-18: Not suitable for transformation. 21 test methods: ~9 potentially transformable (testGetMergeRegions, testAddMergeRegions, testGetRegion, testScanMetaForTable, plus unit tests for parsing), ~12 not transformable (testIsMetaWhenAllHealthy uses getMaster().waitForMetaOnline(), testIsMetaWhenMetaGoesOffline uses getMaster/getRegionServer, testMetaUpdatesGoToPriorityQueue uses custom RSRpcServices class and scheduler internals, testScanByRegionEncodedNameExistingRegion uses getHBaseCluster().getRegions()). Transformable tests are mostly MetaTableAccessor API correctness tests (internal API, not client-facing) - many are unit tests not requiring a cluster. Unique/valuable tests (meta priority queue, meta failover timing) require direct server access. Not worth partial transformation - MetaTableAccessor correctness tests don't provide upgrade test value. |
| 🔄 | TestMovedRegionCache | Rechecked 2025-11-18: Confirmed not transformable. Single test method validates moved region cache (internal RS optimization for redirecting clients after region moves). Requires: (1) cluster.getRegionServer(0)/getRegionServer(1) to get HRegionServer references (ProcessBased doesn't provide), (2) source.getOnlineRegion(regionName) to check if region is hosted locally (server-internal method, no client API), (3) source.getMovedRegion(encodedName) to query moved region cache entries (in-memory JVM cache, no client API), (4) source.movedRegionCacheExpiredTime() to read cache expiration config (internal method). Moved region cache is invisible to clients - purely internal performance optimization. Test validates cache creation on move, expiration timing, and cleanup. Zero client-visible behavior to test. |
| ✅ | TestMultiVersions | Successfully transformed with 9 checkpoints (testScanMultipleVersions, testGetRowVersions). Compilation passed. |
| ✅ | TestNamespace | Reduced version: 7 test methods (verifyReservedNS, testDeleteReservedNS, createRemoveTest, createDoubleTest, createTableTest, createTableInDefaultNamespace, createTableInSystemNamespace, testNamespaceOperations). ZKNamespaceManager and MasterFileSystem verifications removed (require internal access). All namespace operations tested via Admin API. 16 checkpoints total. Compilation passed. |
| 🔄 | TestRegionRebalancing | Rechecked 2025-11-18: Confirmed not transformable. Single test method validates region rebalancing during dynamic cluster scaling. Test flow: (1) Start with 1 RS, (2) Add RS via startRegionServer() (no args) - total 2, (3) Add another RS - total 3, (4) Kill 1 RS - total 2, (5) Add 2 more RS - total 4, (6) Add 6 more RS - total 10. Calls getMaster().balance() and verifies region distribution (getMaster().getServerManager().areDeadServersInProgress(), getOnlineRegionServers() via getRegionServerThreads(), server.getRSRpcServices()). ProcessBasedMiniHBaseCluster does NOT support startRegionServer() without args - can only specify fixed server count via Builder at creation time, then restart/stop/kill existing servers. Cannot dynamically add new servers beyond initial count. Test's core value is validating cluster growth scenarios, which ProcessBased cannot support. Reduced version would only test restart/kill of existing servers, fundamentally different from cluster scaling. |
| 🔄 | TestSequenceIdMonotonicallyIncreasing | Rechecked 2025-11-18: Confirmed not transformable. 2 test methods validate WAL sequence ID monotonicity during split/merge (HBASE-20066). testSplit(): (1) Write data, flush, (2) Split region, (3) Read WAL file to find max sequence ID for original region, (4) Verify new regions have seqNum = maxSeqId + 1. testMerge(): Similar for merge. Requires: (1) rs.getWAL(null) to get WAL instance from HRegionServer (server-internal), (2) Cast to AbstractFSWAL and call getCurrentFileName() to get WAL file path, (3) NoEOFWALStreamReader.create() to open WAL file, (4) reader.next() to read WAL entries, (5) entry.getKey().getSequenceId() to extract internal sequence IDs, (6) cluster.getRegions(NAME) to get HRegion instances, (7) cluster.getServerWith() to find hosting server. Tests internal WAL correctness - no client API exposes WAL files, entries, or sequence IDs. |
