| 🔄 | TestZooKeeper | Rechecked 2025-11-18: Confirmed not transformable. 5 test methods validate ZK session management and recovery: (1) testRegionServerSessionExpired - calls TEST_UTIL.expireRegionServerSession(0) then verifies cluster sanity, (2) testMasterSessionExpired - calls TEST_UTIL.expireMasterSession(), (3) testMasterZKSessionRecoveryFailure - gets HMaster via getMaster(), calls m.abort() directly, checks m.isStopped(), (4) testRegionAssignmentAfterMasterRecoveryDueToZKExpiry - uses cluster.startRegionServer() and custom MockLoadBalancer with static boolean retainAssignCalled to track internal assignment logic. Requires: (1) expireRegionServerSession/expireMasterSession - manipulates in-process ZKWatcher, impossible across separate ProcessBased JVMs, (2) Custom MockLoadBalancer class with static state - cannot inject into separate ProcessBased master JVM, static fields not shared across processes, (3) Direct HMaster access for abort() and isStopped(), (4) Dynamic server addition. Cannot simulate ZK session expiration or track custom balancer state across process boundaries. |

