| ❌ | TestReplicationStatusSourceStartedTargetStoppedNewOp | Tests replication load metrics when source is restarted but target is stopped with new operations. Extends TestReplicationBase requiring multi-cluster setup (UTIL1/UTIL2). Requires: (1) UTIL2.shutdownMiniHBaseCluster() to stop peer cluster (line 48), (2) restartSourceCluster(1) from base class (line 49), (3) Direct HRegionServer access via UTIL1.getHBaseCluster().getRegionServer(0).getServerName() (line 58). Tests verify normal (non-recovery) queue metrics when target cluster is down and source has new operations (hasEditsSinceRestart, timestampOfLastShippedOp=0, replicationLag>0, isRecovered=false). ProcessBasedMiniHBaseCluster does not support multi-cluster setup required for cross-cluster replication testing. Same limitations as other TestReplicationBase subclasses. |
| ❌ | TestReplicationStatusSourceStartedTargetStoppedNoOps | Tests replication load metrics when source is restarted but target is stopped with no new operations. Extends TestReplicationBase requiring multi-cluster setup (UTIL1/UTIL2). Requires: (1) UTIL2.shutdownMiniHBaseCluster() to stop peer cluster (line 45), (2) restartSourceCluster(1) from base class (line 46), (3) Direct HRegionServer access via UTIL1.getHBaseCluster().getRegionServer(0).getServerName() (line 48). Tests verify empty queue metrics when target cluster is down and source has no new operations (hasEditsSinceRestart=false, timestampOfLastShippedOp=0, replicationLag=0, isRecovered=false). ProcessBasedMiniHBaseCluster does not support multi-cluster setup required for cross-cluster replication testing. Same limitations as other TestReplicationBase subclasses. |
| ❌ | TestReplicationStatusSourceStartedTargetStoppedWithRecovery | Tests replication load metrics when source is restarted with recovery queue while target is stopped. Extends TestReplicationBase requiring multi-cluster setup (UTIL1/UTIL2). Requires: (1) UTIL2.shutdownMiniHBaseCluster() to stop peer cluster (line 49), writes data before restart (lines 51-55), (2) restartSourceCluster(1) from base class to create recovery queue (line 57), (3) Direct HRegionServer access via UTIL1.getHBaseCluster().getRegionServer(0).getServerName() (line 59). Tests verify both normal and recovery queue metrics when target cluster is down (recovery queue: hasEditsSinceRestart=true, replicationLag>0; normal queue: hasEditsSinceRestart=false, replicationLag=0). ProcessBasedMiniHBaseCluster does not support multi-cluster setup required for cross-cluster replication testing. Same limitations as other TestReplicationBase subclasses. |
| ❌ | TestReplicationSyncUpToolBase | Base class for ReplicationSyncUp tool tests with no @Test methods. Sets up multi-cluster infrastructure with two HBaseTestingUtility instances (UTIL1, UTIL2) managing separate MiniHBaseCluster clusters (lines 42-43, 77-78). Uses TestReplicationBase.configureClusters() for cross-cluster replication setup (line 73). Requires UTIL1.startMiniZKCluster() and UTIL2.setZkCluster() for shared ZK cluster setup (lines 74-75). Not a standalone test class - serves as parent for ReplicationSyncUp tool test classes. Subclasses require same multi-cluster setup. ProcessBasedMiniHBaseCluster does not support multi-cluster setup required for cross-cluster replication testing. |
| ❌ | TestSerialReplication | Tests serial replication functionality (HBASE-9465). Extends SerialReplicationTestBase requiring extensive internal access. SerialReplicationTestBase requires: (1) Direct RegionServerThread access via getLiveRegionServerThreads() for WAL rolling (base lines 172-173, 179-180), (2) getWalRoller().requestRollAll() and walRollRequestFinished() for WAL internals (base lines 173, 180), (3) Direct WAL file reading via NoEOFWALStreamReader to verify replication order and sequence IDs (base lines 195-246), (4) Direct region access via rs.getRegion() (base line 161). Tests verify serial replication maintains order of edits during replication. ProcessBasedMiniHBaseCluster does not support RegionServerThread/WAL access across process boundaries. Cannot access WAL files, walRoller, or verify internal sequence ID ordering. Similar limitations as TestAddToSerialReplicationPeer and TestRemoveFromSerialReplicationPeer. |
| ❌ | TestSerialReplicationFailover | Tests serial replication failover behavior during RegionServer failures. Extends SerialReplicationTestBase requiring same extensive internal access. Tests verify serial replication order is maintained when region servers fail and replication queues are recovered. SerialReplicationTestBase requires: (1) Direct RegionServerThread access via getLiveRegionServerThreads() for WAL rolling, (2) getWalRoller().requestRollAll() and walRollRequestFinished() for WAL internals, (3) Direct WAL file reading via NoEOFWALStreamReader to verify sequence ID ordering after failover, (4) Direct region access via rs.getRegion(). ProcessBasedMiniHBaseCluster does not support RegionServerThread/WAL access across process boundaries. Cannot access WAL files or verify internal replication queue recovery. Same limitations as TestSerialReplication and other SerialReplicationTestBase subclasses. |

